{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nTask SE-PE-01: Grammar-guided node reduction (Perses-style)\n\nThe rules are:\n1. Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes (process deeper nodes first)\n2. Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children\n3. Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\n4. Use node ID as stable tie-break at equal depth\n5. Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order\n\nLet me think through the algorithm:\n\n1. Build the tree structure from the nodes list\n2. Process nodes in order: deeper first, tie-break by node ID (lexicographic? or by position?)\n3. For each node (candidate for removal):\n   - Skip if not removable\n   - Skip if it's the root\n   - Skip if its symbol is in required_symbols\n   - Skip if it has any retained children\n   - Tentatively remove it and check if all required symbols are still represented\n   - If yes, remove it; otherwise keep it\n\nWait, let me re-read: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\"\n\nSo conditions to NOT remove:\n- node is root (parent is null)\n- node's symbol is in required_symbols\n- node has retained children (children that haven't been removed yet)\n\nAnd additionally: \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\"\n\nThe order: deeper nodes first, tie-break by node ID.\n\nFor the tie-break \"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth\" - node IDs are strings like \"root\", \"n1\", \"n2\", etc. Lexicographic order would be: n1 \u003c n2 \u003c n3 \u003c n4 \u003c n5 \u003c n6 \u003c root. But wait, \"root\" lexicographically comes after \"n\" strings... actually 'r' \u003e 'n' so root would be last alphabetically among these.\n\nActually for the same depth, we want to process them in some order. Let me think about what \"stable tie break\" means - it just means we process in a deterministic order. Lexicographic by node ID seems right.\n\nLet me trace through case 0:\n- Nodes: root(depth 0), n1(depth 1, s1, not removable), n2(depth 1, s2, removable), n3(depth 1, s0, not removable), n4(depth 2, s1, removable, parent n2), n5(depth 2, s2, not removable, parent n3), n6(depth 2, s0, removable, parent n1)\n- required_symbols: [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n\nProcess order (depth descending, then node ID):\n- Depth 2: n4, n5, n6 (sorted by ID: n4, n5, n6)\n- Depth 1: n1, n2, n3 (sorted by ID: n1, n2, n3)\n- Depth 0: root\n\nTry n4 (depth 2, s1, removable):\n- Not root ✓\n- Symbol s1 IS in required_symbols → cannot remove\n\nTry n5 (depth 2, s2, not removable):\n- Not removable → skip\n\nTry n6 (depth 2, s0, removable):\n- Not root ✓\n- Symbol s0 not in required_symbols ✓\n- No children (depth 2, and there are no depth 3 nodes) ✓\n- If removed, remaining symbols: root(root), n1(s1), n2(s2, but only if n2 is retained), n3(s0), n5(s2)... wait, we need to check if all required symbols remain represented in the RETAINED set\n- Current retained = {root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5, n6} - {n6} = {root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5}\n- Symbols in retained: root, s1, s2, s0, s1, s2 → includes \"root\" and \"s1\" ✓\n- Remove n6! removal_order = [n6]\n\nTry n1 (depth 1, s1, not removable):\n- Not removable → skip\n\nTry n2 (depth 1, s2, removable):\n- Not root ✓\n- Symbol s2 not in required_symbols ✓\n- Has retained children? n4 is a child of n2. Is n4 retained? Yes (we couldn't remove n4 because its symbol is required)\n- n4 is retained → cannot remove n2\n\nTry n3 (depth 1, s0, not removable):\n- Not removable → skip\n\nTry root (depth 0):\n- Is root (parent null) → cannot remove\n\nFinal state:\n- removed: [n6]\n- retained: [root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5] (sorted)\n\nSo removed_node_ids = [\"n6\"] (in removal order)\nretained_node_ids = sorted([\"root\", \"n1\", \"n2\", \"n3\", \"n4\", \"n5\"])\n\nFor sorting retained_node_ids - \"sorted\" means lexicographic? Let's check: n1, n2, n3, n4, n5, root → lexicographic: n1, n2, n3, n4, n5, root (since 'n' \u003c 'r')\n\nNow let me implement this:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Validate required fields\n    if not isinstance(nodes, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"nodes must be a list\")\n    if not isinstance(case[\"required_symbols\"], list):\n        raise ValueError(\"required_symbols must be a list\")\n    \n    # Build node map\n    node_map = {}\n    for node in nodes:\n        for field in (\"id\", \"parent\", \"symbol\", \"depth\", \"removable\", \"utility\"):\n            if field not in node:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Node missing field: {field}\")\n        node_map[node[\"id\"]] = node\n    \n    # Build children map\n    children = {nid: [] for nid in node_map}\n    root_id = None\n    for node in nodes:\n        if node[\"parent\"] is None:\n            root_id = node[\"id\"]\n        else:\n            if node[\"parent\"] not in node_map:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Parent {node['parent']} not found\")\n            children[node[\"parent\"]].append(node[\"id\"])\n    \n    if root_id is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"No root node found\")\n    \n    # Sort nodes by depth descending, then node ID ascending (lexicographic)\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    # Track retained set\n    retained = set(node_map.keys())\n    removed_order = []\n    \n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        \n        # Skip if not removable\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Skip if root\n        if node[\"parent\"] is None:\n            continue\n        \n        # Skip if symbol is required\n        if node[\"symbol\"] in required_symbols:\n            continue\n        \n        # Skip if has retained children\n        has_retained_children = any(c in retained for c in children[nid])\n        if has_retained_children:\n            continue\n        \n        # Check if all required symbols remain if we remove this node\n        tentative_retained = retained - {nid}\n        symbols_in_retained = {node_map[n][\"symbol\"] for n in tentative_retained}\n        if required_symbols.issubset(symbols_in_retained):\n            retained = tentative_retained\n            removed_order.append(nid)\n    \n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_sorted\n    }\n```\n\nLet me trace through case 0 again with this code:\n\nNodes sorted by (-depth, id):\n- depth 2: n4, n5, n6\n- depth 1: n1, n2, n3\n- depth 0: root\n\nn4: removable=True, parent=n2 (not None), symbol=s1 (in required_symbols) → skip\n\nn5: removable=False → skip\n\nn6: removable=True, parent=n1 (not None), symbol=s0 (not required), no children → check\n- tentative_retained = {root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5}\n- symbols = {root, s1, s2, s0, s1, s2} = {root, s1, s2, s0}\n- required = {root, s1} ⊆ {root, s1, s2, s0} ✓\n- Remove n6! removed_order = [\"n6\"]\n\nn1: removable=False → skip\n\nn2: removable=True, parent=root, symbol=s2, children=[n4], n4 in retained → has_retained_children=True → skip\n\nn3: removable=False → skip\n\nroot: parent=None → skip\n\nResult:\n- removed_node_ids: [\"n6\"]\n- retained_node_ids: sorted([\"root\", \"n1\", \"n2\", \"n3\", \"n4\", \"n5\"]) = [\"n1\", \"n2\", \"n3\", \"n4\", \"n5\", \"root\"]\n\nCase 1 trace:\nNodes: root(0,root,not-rem), n1(1,s1,not-rem), n2(1,s2,rem), n3(1,s0,not-rem), n4(2,s1,rem,parent=n2), n5(2,s2,not-rem,parent=n3), n6(2,s0,rem,parent=n1)\nrequired_symbols: {root, s1}\n\nOrder: n4, n5, n6, n1, n2, n3, root\n\nn4: symbol=s1 in required → skip\nn5: not removable → skip\nn6: removable, parent=n1, symbol=s0, no children\n- tentative = {root,n1,n2,n3,n4,n5}\n- symbols = {root,s1,s2,s0,s1,s2} includes root,s1 ✓\n- Remove n6! removed_order=[\"n6\"]\n\nn1: not removable → skip\nn2: removable, parent=root, symbol=s2, children=[n4], n4 retained → skip\nn3: not removable → skip\nroot: parent=None → skip\n\nResult: removed=[\"n6\"], retained=sorted({root,n1,n2,n3,n4,n5})\n\nCase 2 trace:\nSimilar structure. n4(s1,rem), n5(s2,not-rem), n6(s0,rem), n1(s1,not-rem), n2(s2,rem), n3(s0,not-rem)\n\nn4: symbol=s1 in required → skip\nn5: not removable → skip\nn6: removable, symbol=s0, no children\n- tentative = {root,n1,n2,n3,n4,n5}\n- symbols include root,s1 ✓\n- Remove n6!\n\nn1: not removable → skip\nn2: removable, children=[n4] retained → skip\nn3: not removable → skip\nroot: skip\n\nResult: removed=[\"n6\"], retained=[\"n1\",\"n2\",\"n3\",\"n4\",\"n5\",\"root\"]\n\nAll three cases seem consistent. The implementation looks correct.\n\nNow I need to format this as the required JSON output with the \"implementation\" key containing the Python source as a string.\n\nLet me write the final Python code cleanly and then JSON-encode it.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    required_symbols = set(case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"])\\n\\n    if not isinstance(nodes, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"nodes must be a list\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"], list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"required_symbols must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    node_map = {}\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        for field in (\\\"id\\\", \\\"parent\\\", \\\"symbol\\\", \\\"depth\\\", \\\"removable\\\", \\\"utility\\\"):\\n            if field not in node:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Node missing field: {field}\\\")\\n        node_map[node[\\\"id\\\"]] = node\\n\\n    children = {nid: [] for nid in node_map}\\n    root_id = None\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        if node[\\\"parent\\\"] is None:\\n            if root_id is not None:\\n                raise ValueError(\\\"Multiple root nodes found\\\")\\n            root_id = node[\\\"id\\\"]\\n        else:\\n            if node[\\\"parent\\\"] not in node_map:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Parent {node['parent']!r} not in node map\\\")\\n            children[node[\\\"parent\\\"]].append(node[\\\"id\\\"])\\n\\n    if root_id is None:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"No root node found\\\")\\n\\n    # Process deeper nodes first; tie-break by node ID ascending (lexicographic)\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\\\"depth\\\"], n[\\\"id\\\"]))\\n\\n    retained = set(node_map.keys())\\n    removed_order = []\\n\\n    for node in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = node[\\\"id\\\"]\\n\\n        # Must be explicitly removable\\n        if not node[\\\"removable\\\"]:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Never remove root\\n        if node[\\\"parent\\\"] is None:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Never remove a node whose symbol is required\\n        if node[\\\"symbol\\\"] in required_symbols:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Never remove a node with retained children\\n        if any(c in retained for c in children[nid]):\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Tentatively remove: check all required symbols still represented\\n        tentative = retained - {nid}\\n        symbols_present = {node_map[n][\\\"symbol\\\"] for n in tentative}\\n        if required_symbols.issubset(symbols_present):\\n            retained = tentative\\n            removed_order.append(nid)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removed_order,\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": sorted(retained)\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01XuN9tu38lFb6M2QMbv03sR","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2579,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":11,"output_tokens":3450,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2802},"service_tier":"standard"}}